  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 145 PM EDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\n*** Tomorrow - Monday Night ***\n\nBehind the cold front, a surface high pressure will build into the \nOhio Valley starting tomorrow. The upper level ridge that is \ncurrently in place over the southern Plains will continue to \npersist, leaving the Ohio Valley region in a northwesterly flow \naloft. Tomorrow some gusty winds are possible through the day as a \nmid-level jet moves through. Maximum temperatures tomorrow are \nexpected to be in the mid to low 80s tomorrow with the CAA behind \nthe front. Temperatures will bounce back to the mid to upper 80s by \nSaturday. \n\nThe next chance for precip will be Friday as a shortwave \ntrough moves east from the Central Plains. As we move into the late \nweekend early week, a couple frontal boundaries will move through \nthe region. This will likely bring another round of rain showers for \nSunday into Monday. Temperatures to start the week will be in the \nupper 80s and low 90s.",
